## 2. Feature Gaps I'd Add to the Plan

### 🔍 Phone Lookup Bar (Critical — Add to Sprint 2.1)
When a call comes in, the agent sees a phone number. They need to find the contact **in under 2 seconds**. The current plan has search in the contacts table, but it's buried with other filters.

**Recommendation:** Add a persistent search bar in the `TopBar` (visible on every page). Type a phone number → instant lookup → click to open contact detail. This is the most-used feature in any call center.

### 📦 Bulk Actions (Add to Sprint 2.1)
Agents will ask for these within the first week:
- "Select All Filtered → Change Status"
- "Select 20 contacts → Assign to Agent X" (admin only)
- "Select All → Export CSV"

Add checkboxes to the contacts table and a floating action bar when items are selected.

### 📤 CSV Export (Add to Sprint 2.1 or 4.2)
Admin WILL need to export data. Government grants, ministry reports, donor updates — they all need Excel files. Add a simple "Export Filtered Contacts" button that generates a CSV with the current filter applied.

### 🔁 Duplicate Detection (Add to Sprint 2.2)
When creating a contact manually, check if a contact with the same phone number already exists. Show a warning: "A contact with this phone already exists: [Name]. View existing contact?"

This prevents the biggest data quality headache in call centers.

### ⏭️ "Next Contact" Flow (Add to Sprint 3.1)
After logging a call, instead of just closing the modal, offer:
- "Next Contact" button → opens the next assigned contact with status "New" or oldest pending follow-up
- This creates a natural call queue without needing a separate queue system

### ⌨️ Keyboard Shortcuts (Add to Sprint 7.1)
Call center agents are speed-oriented. At minimum:
- `/` → Focus search bar
- `Esc` → Close any modal
- `N` → New contact (when not in an input)
- `L` → Log call (from contact detail)

### 🖨️ Print View (Add to Sprint 5.2)
Ministry leaders will want to print prayer request lists for group prayer sessions. Add a "Print" button on the prayer requests page that opens a clean, printer-friendly view.

