## 3. Supabase Free Tier — Things That Will Bite You

| Concern | Limit | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| Database size | 500 MB | With <1000 contacts + audit logs, you're fine for ~6 months |
| Auth MAUs | 50,000 | Not an issue with a few agents |
| File storage | 1 GB | Only relevant if you add profile photos later |
| **No daily backups** | ❌ | **This is the big one.** If data is corrupted or deleted, it's gone |
| Edge functions | 500K/month | Not using edge functions, so no issue |
| Bandwidth | 5 GB | Fine for a data-centric app |

### 🛡️ Backup Strategy (DO THIS)
Supabase free tier has NO automatic backups. You're collecting prayer requests and ministry data — losing it would be devastating.

**Recommendation:** Create a monthly manual backup routine:
1. Go to Supabase Dashboard → Settings → Database → Download Backup (if available)
2. OR: Add a "Download All Data" button in admin settings that exports every table to JSON/CSV
3. Store backups in Google Drive or a local folder

I can spec this as a mini-sprint if you want.

### 📈 When to Upgrade to Pro ($25/month)
Upgrade when any of these happen:
- More than 500MB database (check in Supabase dashboard → Database → Usage)
- Need daily automatic backups
- Need more than 2 concurrent realtime connections (not relevant yet)
- Need branching for development

