## 7. Pre-Flight Checklist Before Sprint 0.1

Before giving Flash the first sprint, do these manually:

- [ ] **Create Supabase project** at [supabase.com](https://supabase.com) — pick a region (Mumbai `ap-south-1` is closest to India)
- [ ] **Copy the project URL and anon key** from Settings → API
- [ ] **Copy the service role key** (keep it secret, never commit to git)
- [ ] **Create a GitHub repo** (private) for the project
- [ ] **Have Node.js 18+ installed** (`node --version`)
- [ ] **Have npm 9+ installed** (`npm --version`)
- [ ] **Have Git configured** (`git config user.name` and `git config user.email`)

Only then hand Sprint 0.1 to Flash.

---

## 8. My Recommended Order of Operations

```
You (manual)     → Create Supabase project, copy keys
Flash (Sprint 0.1) → Scaffold Next.js app
You (manual)     → Add .env.local with real keys, verify app runs
Flash (Sprint 1.1) → Auth + profiles
You (manual)     → Create first admin account in Supabase dashboard
You (manual)     → Run SQL to set role = 'admin'
Flash (Sprint 1.2) → Generate schema SQL
You (manual)     → Run ALL SQL in Supabase SQL Editor in order
You (manual)     → RLS test protocol (critical!)
Flash (Sprint 2.x) → Contacts UI
Me (Opus)        → Review code for design drift, RLS issues
... continue pattern ...
```

The key insight: **You are the glue between Flash and the infrastructure.** Flash can't create Supabase projects, run SQL in dashboards, or set Vercel env vars. Those are your manual steps.
